      "content": "That sounds like a very intense and unusual sensory experience while practicing your phonetics. What you're describing—a sharp, biting, or gnawing sensation with the /s/ sound—is quite vivid. While I can't give you a medical diagnosis, these strong visceral feelings are sometimes related to the precise muscular tension and airflow required to produce certain fricatives like /s/. It's possible your articulators are engaging in a very specific, perhaps slightly strained, manner to create that high-frequency turbulence. You might want to consult a speech-language pathologist to see if they can help you relax the musculature while maintaining the correct airflow.",
      "source": "target",
