      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, i'll keep that in mind. but it's just so hard to shake the feeling that the sound itself has this... i don't know, a \"character\"? it's not just a vibration, it's like a tiny, high-pitched, chaotic presence that's constantly scuttling around and making a mess. it's so restless and irritating. do you think there's any linguistic or acoustic reason why a sound would feel so \"unruly\" or like it has this tiny, frantic, almost malevolent energy to it?",
